<header><h1>The Vuil&rsquo;raith Cabal</h1></header>
<article>
<h2 id="devour"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Vuil&#x27;Raith_Cabal#:~:text=Devour">Devour</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>When an opponent&rsquo;s Infantry II is destroyed during combat, the Vuil&rsquo;raith player captures an infantry token, and the opponent rolls for resurrection, placing the destroyed infantry on the Infantry II unit upgrade card if successful.<sup>4</sup></li>
    <li>The Vuil&rsquo;raith player cannot capture the <a href="/F_ul">Ul</a> player&rsquo;s Hel Titan PDS.<sup>2</sup></li>
    <li>Units destroyed by <a href="/R_space_cannon"><sc>Space Cannon</sc></a> or <a href="/R_bombardment"><sc>Bombardment</sc></a> rolls are not destroyed during combat, and are not captured by <sc>Devour</sc>. Units destroyed by <a href="/R_anti_fighter_barrage"><sc>Anti&ndash;Fighter Barrage</sc></a> are destroyed during combat, and are captured.<sup>2</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="amalgamation"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Vuil&#x27;Raith_Cabal#:~:text=Amalgamation">Amalgamation</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>If the Vuil&rsquo;raith player produces multiple units, their <sc>Amalgamation</sc> ability may be applied to each.<sup>2</sup></li>
    <li>If the Vuil&rsquo;raith player has captured their own units, they may use their <sc>Amalgamation</sc> ability when producing a unit of that type, even if they have no other units of that type in their reinforcements.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li><sc>Amalgamation</sc> does not change the cost of the produced units, only the resources spent.<sup>2</sup></li>
    <ol><li>If the Vuil&rsquo;raith player uses the ability of the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Cybernetic_Technologies#Integrated_Economy"><i>Integrated Economy</i></a> technology, <sc>Amalgamation</sc> will have no effect on the limit to the units they may build.<sup>2</sup></li></ol>
    <li>The Vuil&rsquo;raith player produces one fighter or infantry without spending resources for each captured fighter or infantry they spend.<sup>2</sup></li>
    <li>If the Vuil&rsquo;raith player has the <a href="/F_naalu">Naalu</a> or <a href="/F_yin">Yin</a> player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Promissory_Notes#Alliance"><i>Alliance</i></a> promissory note, they may spend one resource for one fighter or infantry, but spend a captured unit instead of that resource, then get one additional fighter or infantry for no cost, which will not count toward their production limit.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li>A captured faction&ndash;specific unit counts as a unit of its base type; for example, a captured <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Embers_of_Muaat#War_Sun:~:text=Prototype%20War%20Sun">Prototype War Sun</a> counts as a war sun.<sup>2</sup></li>
    <li>The Vuil&rsquo;raith player cannot produce a war sun using <sc>Amalgamation</sc> unless they own their war sun unit upgrade technology.<sup>2</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="riftmeld"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Vuil&#x27;Raith_Cabal#:~:text=Riftmeld">Riftmeld</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The returned captured unit may belong to any player, regardless of whether that player owns the corresponding unit upgrade.<sup>2</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="crucible"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Vuil&#x27;Raith_Cabal#:~:text=Crucible">Crucible</a> <sub>(Promissory Note)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>Each gravity rift will still provide its usual +1 to each ship&rsquo;s move value.<sup>2,4</sup></li>
    <li><i>Crucible</i> will provide an additional +1 to each ship&rsquo;s move value, which will not increase if that ship moves through two or more gravity rifts.<sup>2</sup></li>
    <ol>
        <li>A ship that moves through or out of no gravity rifts will apply +0 to its move value.<sup>*</sup></li>
        <li>A ship that moves through or out of two gravity rifts will apply +3 to its move value.<sup>*</sup></li>
        <li>A ship that moves through or out of three gravity rifts will apply +4 to its move value.<sup>*</sup></li>
        <li>And so on.<sup>*</sup></li>
    </ol>
    <li>If a ship could move from its current system to the active system through a gravity rift if its move value were +2, it may do so using <i>Crucible</i>. This is true even if that ship could not reach the gravity rift without <i>Crucible</i>.<sup>4</sup></li>
    <ol><li>For example, consider a series of systems X&ndash;S&ndash;G&ndash;Y. Only systems connected by a &ldquo;&ndash;&rdquo; are adjacent. System &ldquo;G&rdquo; is a gravity rift. Systems &ldquo;X&rdquo;, &ldquo;S&rdquo; and &ldquo;Y&rdquo; are standard systems with no movement restrictions. A ship with a move value of one is in system &ldquo;X&rdquo;. Were it to have +2 to its movement value, it could reach system &ldquo;Y&rdquo;. Currently, that ship may reach only system &ldquo;S&rdquo;. Despite this, if its owner activated system &ldquo;Y&rdquo; and played <i>Crucible</i>, the ship could move to that system.<sup>4</sup></li></ol>
    <li>If a player plays both <i>Crucible</i> and the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Codex_I:~:text=Nav%20Suite"><i>Nav Suite</i></a> action card during the same tactical action, they will still apply +1 to the move value of their ships that move through or out of a gravity rift.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <ol><li>This +1 comes from the effect of <i>Crucible</i>. The gravity rift itself does not give its +1 because of <i>Nav Suite</i>.<sup>*</sup></li></ol>
    </ol>

<h2 id="vortex"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Vuil&#x27;Raith_Cabal#:~:text=Vortex">Vortex</a> <sub>(Technology)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li><i>Vortex</i> cannot be used if there are no units that can be targeted.<sup>4</sup></li>
    <li>If a player has all their units of a particular type on the board, other than fighters or infantry, that type of unit belonging to that player cannot be targeted.<sup>4</sup></li>
    <li>If another player is blockading a <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Vuil&#x27;Raith_Cabal#:~:text=Dimensional%20Tear">Dimensional Tear</a>, their units cannot be targeted with <i>Vortex</i>.<sup>8</sup></li>
    <li><i>Vortex</i> cannot target the <a href="/F_ul">Ul</a> player&rsquo;s Hel Titan, as it is a structure.<sup>2</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="dimensional-tear"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Vuil&#x27;Raith_Cabal#:~:text=Dimensional%20Tear">Dimensional Tear</a> <sub>(Unit)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>A system containing a Dimensional Tear is an anomaly.<sup>2,4</sup></li>
    <ol><li>This system qualifies for the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Objectives#Prophecy_of_Kings_Expansion:~:text=Make%20History"><i>Make History</i></a> and similar such objectives.<sup>2</sup></li></ol>
    <li>If a ship moves through or out of the same gravity rift multiple times, that gravity rift provides +1 to its move value only once, but the ship rolls for removal each time.<sup>6,7</sup></li>
    <li>Multiple Dimensional Tears in a single system have no additional effects.<sup>2</sup></li>
    <li>If a Dimensional Tear is in a system that is normally a gravity rift (e.g. the Cormund system), the Vuil&rsquo;raith player will not have to roll for removal when moving out of or through that system. There are no additional effects.<sup>2</sup></li>
    <li>If the <a href="/F_nekro">Nekro</a> player has copied Dimensional Tear II, systems containing the <a href="/F_nekro">Nekro</a> player&rsquo;s space docks are gravity rifts for the Vuil&rsquo;raith player&rsquo;s ships. The Vuil&rsquo;raith player must roll for removal for each ship that moves out of or through those systems.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li>If a Dimensional Tear is in a system with a Nebula, then the +1 to move values will be applied after the nebula sets each ship&rsquo;s move value to 1.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li>If the Dimensional Tear plastic figure is destroyed, the Dimensional Tear token is also removed.<sup>8</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="the-terror-between"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Vuil&#x27;Raith_Cabal#:~:text=The%20Terror%20Between">The Terror Between</a> <sub>(Flagship)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>When <i>The Terror Between</i> is destroyed, it still captures units that were destroyed at the same time.<sup>2,4</sup></li>
    <ol><li>Using the <a href="/R_sustain_damage"><sc>Sustain Damage</sc></a> ability of units is done before remaining hits are assigned. As such, if <i>The Terror Between</i> is destroyed by a <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition:~:text=Direct%20Hit"><i>Direct Hit</i></a> action card, units destroyed by being assigned hits in the same round of combat, or from the same pool of <a href="/R_space_cannon"><sc>Space Cannon</sc></a> hits, will not be captured.<sup>*</sup></li></ol>
    <li>If ships are destroyed outside of combat, those ships will still be captured by <i>The Terror Between</i>.<sup>2</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="the-stillness-of-stars"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Vuil&#x27;Raith_Cabal#:~:text=The%20Stillness%20of%20Stars">The Stillness of Stars</a> <sub>(Agent)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>If a player loses their commodities immediately after replenishing them, most commonly via that player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Promissory_Notes#Trade_Agreement"><i>Trade Agreement</i></a> promissory note, the Vuil&rsquo;raith player may still target them. If they do, they still use that player&rsquo;s full commodity value to determine which units may be captured.<sup>4</sup></li>
    <li>The Vuil&rsquo;raith player cannot capture a unit without a cost. Notably, they cannot capture a PDS, a space dock, or a war sun of a player without their war sun unit upgrade.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li>If the Vuil&rsquo;raith player chooses to capture a fighter or infantry, they will capture one, not two.<sup>2</sup></li>
    <li>When the primary ability of the <a href="/R_trade"><i>Trade</i></a> strategy card is resolved, the Vuil&rsquo;raith player must choose if they will use The Stillness of Stars or not after the active player has replenished their commodities, but before players are chosen to perform the secondary ability without spending a command token.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li>When the secondary ability of the <a href="/R_trade"><i>Trade</i></a> strategy card is resolved, the Vuil&rsquo;raith player must choose if they will use The Stillness of Stars or not after the current player has replenished their commodities, but before the next player has decided if they will spend a command token to perform the secondary.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li>When The Stillness of Stars converts a player&rsquo;s commodities to trade goods, those trade goods are not treated as being gained for the purpose of triggering other abilities. In particular, the <a href="/F_mentak">Mentak</a> player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Vuil&#x27;Raith_Cabal#:~:text=Pillage"><sc>Pillage</sc></a> faction ability is not triggered by this ability.<sup>4</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="that-which-molds-flesh"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Vuil&#x27;Raith_Cabal#:~:text=That%20Which%20Molds%20Flesh">That Which Molds Flesh</a> <sub>(Commander)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    </ol>

<h2 id="it-feeds-on-carrion"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Vuil&#x27;Raith_Cabal#:~:text=It%20Feeds%20on%20Carrion">It Feeds on Carrion</a> &mdash; <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Vuil&#x27;Raith_Cabal#:~:text=Dimensional%20Anchor">Dimensional Anchor</a><sub> (Hero)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>Units captured while resolving <i>Dimensional Anchor</i> are not destroyed.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li>If a player&rsquo;s units are blockading one of the Vuil&rsquo;raith player&rsquo;s Dimensional Tears, dice will not be rolled for that player&rsquo;s units when resolving <i>Dimensional Anchor</i>.<sup>8</sup></li>
    <li>Each non&ndash;fighter ship affected will roll only once, regardless of how many Dimensional Tears it is adjacent to.<sup>2</sup></li>
    <li>Units can only be captured by the dice specifically allocated to them.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li>If a ship with capacity is captured, its owner chooses which excess fighters and ground forces are removed; they are not assigned to particular ships.<sup>1</sup></li>
    <li>If the <a href="/F_nekro">Nekro</a> player has used a <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nekro_Virus#Faction_Technologies:~:text=Valefar%20Assimilator"><i>Valefar Assimilator</i></a> faction technology to copy <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Vuil&#x27;Raith_Cabal#:~:text=Dimensional%20Tear">Dimensional Tear</a> II, ships in systems containing or adjacent to the <a href="/F_nekro">Nekro</a> player&rsquo;s space docks will also have to roll for capture when resolving <i>Dimensional Anchor</i>. This includes the <a href="/F_nekro">Nekro</a> player&rsquo;s own ships.<sup>*</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="reanimator"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Vuil&#x27;Raith_Cabal#:~:text=Reanimator">Reanimator</a> <sub>(Mech)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>If the Vuil&rsquo;raith player owns the Infantry II unit upgrade technology, and one is destroyed during ground combat on a planet with a Reanimator, the Vuil&rsquo;raith player captures an infantry token, and they roll for resurrection, placing the destroyed infantry on the Infantry II unit upgrade card if successful.<sup>4</sup></li>
    <li>If the Vuil&rsquo;raith player&rsquo;s infantry on a planet with a Reanimator are destroyed outside of combat, such as with the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition:~:text=Plague"><i>Plague</i></a> action card, those infantry will be captured.<sup>*</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="alraith-ix-ianovar"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Vuil&#x27;Raith_Cabal#:~:text=Al%27raith%20Ix%20Ianovar">Al&rsquo;raith Ix Ianovar</a> <sub>(Breakthrough)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The Vuil&rsquo;raith player cannot choose to roll for The Fracture when they gain <i>Al&rsquo;raith Ix Ianovar</i>; the breakthrough&rsquo;s ability replaces the roll.<sup>6</sup></li>
    <li>When The Fracture is brought into play by <i>Al&rsquo;raith Ix Ianovar</i>, the Vuil&rsquo;raith player places ingress tokens according to the synergy on the Cabal breakthrough.<sup>6,9</sup></li>
    <ol>
        <li>This uses the cabal breakthrough synergy colors method, not the one planet per color method.<sup>9</sup></li>
        <li>When <i>Al&rsquo;raith Ix Ianovar</i> causes The Fracture to enter play, all the ingress tokens will be placed before the Vuil&rsquo;raith player chooses which tokens they wish to move into gravity rifts.<sup>*</sup></li>
    </ol>
    <li>The Vuil&rsquo;raith player may move the ingress tokens into systems that contain their Dimensional Tears.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <ol><li>They cannot move an ingress token into a system that already contains an ingress token.<sup>6,7</sup></li></ol>
    <li>Ingress tokens cannot be placed in The Fracture. The Vuil&rsquo;raith player cannot move an ingress token into a system in The Fracture, even if they have a space dock in that system.<sup>6</sup></li>
    </ol>
</article>
